WEBVTT

00:36.825 --> 00:39.567
I was suffocating slowly in the broken shell

00:39.587 --> 00:42.909
Drowning in the static of a burning hell But the

00:42.949 --> 00:45.571
console flickered with a sudden bright green

00:45.731 --> 00:48.652
The cleanest set of numbers that I've ever seen I

00:48.712 --> 00:51.714
recognize a radar, I recognize a code A

00:51.754 --> 00:54.035
transmission coming down the cosmic road

00:57.520 --> 00:59.781
I'm punching in the frequency, I'm opening the

00:59.821 --> 01:02.722
mic Sending out a signal through the heavy metal

01:02.742 --> 01:04.943
strike I'm bleeding out the oxygen, the

01:04.963 --> 01:07.744
temperature is low I need you here right now, I

01:07.764 --> 01:11.665
got nowhere else to go

01:12.265 --> 01:17.867
Mayday, mayday, can you hear me in the deep? I'm

01:17.927 --> 01:22.209
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

01:22.269 --> 01:28.449
keeps Mayday, mayday, I'm burning up the wire

01:29.529 --> 01:33.811
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

01:33.891 --> 01:39.612
fire I receive the telemetry, I'm reading the

01:39.712 --> 01:43.133
line Get here to the dead breach field, we're

01:43.193 --> 01:47.074
running out of time

01:49.843 --> 01:51.984
The radio goes silent, just the hum of the

01:52.025 --> 01:54.306
machine I'm watching the horizon on the

01:54.326 --> 01:56.488
shattered screen Then a shadow blocks the

01:56.508 --> 01:59.410
starlight, massive and wide A heavy rescue

01:59.430 --> 02:02.672
vessel crossing the divide The airlock hisses

02:02.752 --> 02:05.534
and the blast doors part I see my anger coming

02:05.594 --> 02:08.036
with a heavy heart The freight dogs and the

02:08.076 --> 02:09.997
captain stepping through the breach You

02:10.097 --> 02:13.139
brought the whole family right into my reach I'm

02:13.179 --> 02:15.601
punching in the frequency, I'm opening the mic

02:15.841 --> 02:18.162
Sending out a signal through the heavy metal,

02:18.182 --> 02:21.066
strike complete The oxygen the temperature is

02:21.126 --> 02:24.471
low I need you here right now I got nowhere else to

02:24.511 --> 02:24.831
go

02:27.582 --> 02:33.125
Mayday! Mayday! Can you hear me in the deep? I'm

02:33.185 --> 02:37.428
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

02:37.488 --> 02:44.032
keeps Mayday! Mayday! I'm burning up the wire

02:44.712 --> 02:48.955
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

02:49.035 --> 02:54.698
fire I'll receive the telemetry I'm reading the

02:54.798 --> 02:58.281
line. Get here to the debris field. We're

02:58.301 --> 02:59.902
running out of time.

03:45.656 --> 03:48.039
You didn't leave me in the dark

03:51.182 --> 03:53.805
You tracked the signal, you found the spark

03:56.588 --> 03:59.231
The gravity was crushing, the limit was crossed

03:59.271 --> 04:01.694
But the family arrived before the engine was

04:01.774 --> 04:03.756
lost

04:05.334 --> 04:10.836
Mayday, mayday, can you hear me in the deep? I'm

04:10.876 --> 04:15.138
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

04:15.178 --> 04:21.681
keeps Mayday, mayday, I'm burning up the wire

04:22.361 --> 04:26.543
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

04:26.623 --> 04:32.247
fire I receive the telemetry I'm reading the

04:32.387 --> 04:35.790
line. Get here to the debris field. We're

04:35.830 --> 04:38.953
running out of time.

04:41.476 --> 04:43.658
You read the line.

04:47.201 --> 04:52.907
You made the time. The cavalry is here.

